---
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { release, observationsFor, url } from '../../lib/publication';
export function getStaticPaths() { return release.geographies.filter(g => ['state','union_territory','ut'].includes(g.type)).map(g => ({params:{slug:g.slug},props:{geography:g}})); }
const { geography } = Astro.props;
const rows = observationsFor(geography.id);
---
<Site title={`${geography.name} coverage`}><PageHeader title={geography.name} eyebrow="Directory & coverage record" description="A name entry from the reviewed official roster. No state-level water measurement is implied by this directory page." crumbs={[{label:'States & UTs',href:'/states/'},{label:geography.name}]} /><section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="grid-2"><div><p class="eyebrow">Geography</p><h2>What this record covers</h2><p>{geography.type === 'state' ? 'State' : 'Union territory'} · official LGD code {geography.code || 'not yet joined'} · inventory version {geography.version || 'not supplied'}.</p><p>This name is from the <a href="https://www.india.gov.in/calendar?date=2026-09-24">National Portal roster</a>. The URL slug is an internal navigation ID. A district result requires its own source footprint and code; a state figure is not a district measurement.</p></div><div class="empty-panel"><p class="eyebrow">Local coverage</p><div class="numberline"><b>{rows.length}</b><span>approved observations</span></div><p>Service reliability, water quality, groundwater and response documents require separate local evidence.</p></div></div>{rows.length ? <div class="table-wrap"><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Indicator</th><th>Value</th><th>Period</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map(o => <tr><td>{o.metricId.replaceAll('_',' ')}</td><td>{o.value} {o.unit}</td><td>{o.periodStart} to {o.periodEnd}</td><td><a href={url(`/sources/${o.sourceId}/`)}>Evidence record</a></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div> : <div class="note"><strong>No reviewed local measurements.</strong><p>This means coverage is unavailable here, not that conditions are normal.</p></div>}</div></section><section class="section"><div class="shell grid-3"><article class="editorial-card"><h3>Season matters</h3><p>Southwest and northeast monsoons, winter precipitation and water years have different local relevance. No season is selected here without an applicable source.</p></article><article class="editorial-card"><h3>Response</h3><p>No current local notification or service action has been verified for this page.</p><a href={url('/response/')}>How actions are tracked ↗</a></article><article class="editorial-card"><h3>What to check next</h3><p>Look for a dated local utility notice, catchment storage, groundwater measurements and official advisories.</p><a href={url('/data-status/')}>Coverage report ↗</a></article></div></section></Site>
